            <ArticleTitle>Evidence-Based Medicine and the Problem of Healthy Volunteers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>832-834</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5604/01.3001.0010.5272</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Healthy controls are subjects without the disease being studied but may have other conditions indirectly affecting outcome. In the present epidemics of obesity a few subjects with undiagnosed nonalcoholic fatty liver disease enter clinical studies as controls, producing biased results. Stricter selection criteria should be considered to prevent this risk.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
